(function(E){ const x = E["exam-09"] = E["exam-09"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x09-r2"] = {"id":"x09-r2","patterns":["RA-history","GT2-business","GT2-career","PARA-cause","PARA-rules","TR-samewords","TR-detail","TR-paraphrase","TR-limit","TR-plural"],"title":{"en":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","tr":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","fa":"Reading ۲: متن ۲ (Passage 2) / بخش ۲ (Section 2)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find details in lettered sections, choose the two answers that the passage really supports, and complete a short summary with words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste harfli bölümlerde ayrıntı bulmayı, metnin gerçekten desteklediği iki cevabı seçmeyi ve kısa bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جزئیات را در بخش‌های حرف‌دار پیدا کنی، دو جوابی را که متن واقعاً تأیید می‌کند انتخاب کنی و یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete sentences and notes on two pieces of workplace advice, using one word from the text in its exact form.","tr":"Bu derste iş yeriyle ilgili iki tavsiye metninde cümleleri ve notları, metinden tek bir kelimeyi tam biçimiyle kullanarak tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها و یادداشت‌های دو متن توصیه‌ای درباره‌ی محیط کار را با یک کلمه از متن، به همان شکل دقیق، کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 2: a history in sections","tr":"Reading Passage 2: bölümlere ayrılmış bir tarih","fa":"Reading Passage 2: تاریخی در چند بخش"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find details in lettered sections, choose the two answers that the passage really supports, and complete a short summary with words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste harfli bölümlerde ayrıntı bulmayı, metnin gerçekten desteklediği iki cevabı seçmeyi ve kısa bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جزئیات را در بخش‌های حرف‌دار پیدا کنی، دو جوابی را که متن واقعاً تأیید می‌کند انتخاب کنی و یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: smugglers on the coast","tr":"Bu sınav: kıyıdaki kaçakçılar","fa":"این آزمون: قاچاقچی‌های ساحل"},"intro":{"en":"History, archaeology and culture are among the most frequent Academic topics. A history in sections usually moves from causes to methods, people, problems and an ending, so the section letters follow the story.","tr":"Tarih, arkeoloji ve kültür en sık çıkan Academic konular arasındadır. Bölümlere ayrılmış bir tarih genelde nedenlerden yöntemlere, insanlara, sorunlara ve bir sona doğru ilerler; bölüm harfleri hikâyeyi izler.","fa":"تاریخ، باستان‌شناسی و فرهنگ از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌های Academic هستند. تاریخی که در چند بخش آمده معمولاً از علت‌ها به روش‌ها، آدم‌ها، مشکل‌ها و پایان می‌رسد، پس حرف‌های بخش‌ها دنبال داستان‌اند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x09-r2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-history","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A historical trade and why it ended","tr":"Tarihî bir ticaret ve neden sona erdiği","fa":"یک تجارت تاریخی و دلیل پایانش"},"asks":{"en":"A passage in seven lettered sections explains a historical activity: what it was, why it paid, how it worked, who supported it, its violent side, why it was hard to stop and what finally ended it. Questions ask where details are, which two reasons are given, and for a short summary.","tr":"Yedi harfli bölümden oluşan bir metin tarihî bir etkinliği anlatıyor: ne olduğunu, neden kazançlı olduğunu, nasıl işlediğini, kimlerin desteklediğini, şiddet yönünü, neden durdurulmasının zor olduğunu ve sonunda neyin bitirdiğini. Sorular ayrıntıların nerede olduğunu, hangi iki nedenin verildiğini soruyor ve kısa bir özet istiyor.","fa":"متنی در هفت بخش حرف‌دار یک فعالیت تاریخی را توضیح می‌دهد: چه بود، چرا سود داشت، چطور کار می‌کرد، چه کسانی حمایتش می‌کردند، جنبه‌ی خشونت‌آمیزش، چرا متوقف کردنش سخت بود و آخر سر چه چیزی تمامش کرد. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند جزئیات کجاست، کدام دو دلیل آمده، و یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه می‌خواهند."},"fields":["What it was","Why it paid","How it worked","Who took part","Violence","Why it was hard to stop","What ended it"],"words":[{"a":"tax","b":"duty / what the government charged on imports","tr":"vergi","fa":"مالیات، عوارض"},{"a":"cheaper","b":"at a lower price / far more cheaply","tr":"daha ucuz","fa":"ارزان‌تر"},{"a":"hidden","b":"concealed / kept out of sight","tr":"saklanmış","fa":"پنهان‌شده"},{"a":"support","b":"took part / bought / invested","tr":"destek","fa":"حمایت"},{"a":"punish","b":"convict / find guilty","tr":"cezalandırmak","fa":"مجازات کردن"},{"a":"refused","b":"were not willing / would not","tr":"reddetti","fa":"قبول نکرد"},{"a":"turned against","b":"stopped supporting / became hostile to","tr":"... karşı döndü","fa":"علیه ... شد"},{"a":"badly paid","b":"poorly paid / low wages","tr":"düşük maaşlı","fa":"کم‌درآمد"},{"a":"easy to bribe","b":"would take money to look away","tr":"rüşvete açık","fa":"رشوه‌پذیر"},{"a":"cut","b":"reduced dramatically / lowered","tr":"indirildi","fa":"کاهش یافت"},{"a":"no longer worth it","b":"ceased to be worth the risk","tr":"artık değmez","fa":"دیگر ارزشش را ندارد"},{"a":"gradually","b":"over the following decades / slowly","tr":"yavaş yavaş","fa":"به‌تدریج"}],"traps":[{"en":"Same words, different idea: \"suddenly\" and \"almost overnight\" describe tea only; for other goods the change was gradual. Check what each phrase refers to.","tr":"Aynı kelimeler, farklı fikir: \"aniden\" ve \"neredeyse bir gecede\" yalnızca çay için geçerli; diğer mallarda değişim yavaştı. Her ifadenin neyi anlattığına bak.","fa":"کلمه‌های یکسان، ایده‌ی متفاوت: «ناگهان» و «تقریباً یک‌شبه» فقط درباره‌ی چای است؛ برای کالاهای دیگر تغییر تدریجی بود. ببین هر عبارت به چه چیزی برمی‌گردد."},{"en":"In choose TWO, wrong options can sound reasonable (\"the courts were far away\") but are simply not in the passage.","tr":"İKİ seçmeli sorularda yanlış seçenekler mantıklı görünebilir (\"mahkemeler uzaktı\") ama metinde hiç yoktur.","fa":"در سؤال‌های «دو تا انتخاب کن»، گزینه‌های غلط ممکن است منطقی به نظر برسند («دادگاه‌ها دور بودند»)، اما اصلاً در متن نیستند."},{"en":"Matching information asks for a detail (a list, a comparison, a reason), not the topic of a whole section.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirme bir bölümün konusunu değil, bir ayrıntıyı (bir liste, bir karşılaştırma, bir neden) sorar.","fa":"جور کردن اطلاعات دنبال یک جزئیات است (فهرست، مقایسه، دلیل)، نه موضوع کل یک بخش."}],"example":{"text":"\"The mill closed in 1890. Cheap imports were blamed, but the real cause was the new railway, which took the workers to better-paid jobs in the city.\"","item":"Which TWO reasons does the writer give for the closure? A cheap imports  B workers leaving for better pay  C the railway","answer":"B and C","why":{"en":"Cheap imports were only \"blamed\"; \"the real cause\" was the railway taking workers to better-paid jobs.","tr":"Ucuz ithalat yalnızca \"suçlandı\"; \"asıl neden\" işçileri daha iyi maaşlı işlere götüren demiryoluydu.","fa":"کالای وارداتی ارزان فقط «مقصر دانسته شد»؛ «علت واقعی» راه‌آهن بود که کارگرها را به کارهای پردرآمدتر برد."}}},{"id":"RA-history-p1","ctx":["RA-history"],"title":{"en":"The history of an object, a place or a trade","tr":"Bir nesnenin, yerin ya da ticaretin tarihi","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء، یک مکان یا یک تجارت"},"asks":{"en":"The history of an everyday object, a trade, a building or a discovery: where it began, who developed it, how it spread and how it changed. Statements test dates, people and causes; the notes follow the order of events.","tr":"Gündelik bir nesnenin, bir ticaretin, bir binanın ya da bir keşfin tarihi: nerede başladığı, kimin geliştirdiği, nasıl yayıldığı ve nasıl değiştiği. İfadeler tarihleri, kişileri ve nedenleri sınar; notlar olayların sırasını izler.","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء روزمره، یک تجارت، یک ساختمان یا یک کشف: از کجا شروع شد، چه کسی آن را توسعه داد، چطور گسترش یافت و چطور تغییر کرد. جمله‌ها تاریخ‌ها، آدم‌ها و علت‌ها را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب رویدادها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The material was first used by local farmers.","The design changed in the 18th century.","The inventor made a lot of money from it.","Notes: Origins · Early uses · Spread · Later developments"],"words":[{"a":"invented","b":"developed / came up with","tr":"icat etti","fa":"اختراع کرد"},{"a":"popular","b":"in demand / widely used","tr":"rağbet gören","fa":"پرطرفدار"},{"a":"spread","b":"was taken to / reached","tr":"yayıldı","fa":"گسترش یافت"},{"a":"expensive","b":"costly / only the rich could afford it","tr":"pahalı","fa":"گران"},{"a":"replaced","b":"took the place of / gave way to","tr":"yerini aldı","fa":"جایش را گرفت"},{"a":"soon","b":"within a few years / shortly afterwards","tr":"kısa sürede","fa":"به‌زودی"},{"a":"earlier than","b":"predates / came before","tr":"... -den önce","fa":"زودتر از"},{"a":"made money","b":"profited from / earned","tr":"para kazandı","fa":"پول درآورد"},{"a":"the government","b":"the authorities / the state","tr":"hükümet","fa":"دولت"},{"a":"exported","b":"sold abroad","tr":"ihraç etti","fa":"صادر کرد"},{"a":"remained","b":"continued / was still","tr":"kaldı, sürdü","fa":"باقی ماند"},{"a":"by hand","b":"without machines / manually","tr":"elle","fa":"با دست"}],"traps":[{"en":"NOT GIVEN when the text names a person but says nothing about their money, motives or feelings.","tr":"Metin bir kişinin adını verip parası, amacı ya da duyguları hakkında hiçbir şey söylemiyorsa: NOT GIVEN.","fa":"وقتی متن اسم کسی را می‌آورد ولی درباره‌ی پول، انگیزه یا احساسش چیزی نمی‌گوید: NOT GIVEN."},{"en":"Dates close together: \"first described in 1565, made in factories from 1795\". Match the date to the event.","tr":"Yakın tarihler: \"ilk kez 1565’te tarif edildi, 1795’ten itibaren fabrikada üretildi\". Tarihi olayla eşleştir.","fa":"تاریخ‌های نزدیک هم: «اولین بار ۱۵۶۵ توصیف شد، از ۱۷۹۵ در کارخانه ساخته شد». تاریخ را با رویداد جور کن."}],"example":{"text":"Glass windows were known in Roman times, but for centuries only churches and the very rich could afford them. In 1696 England introduced a tax on windows, and many owners bricked theirs up. The tax was finally abolished in 1851.","item":"Notes: Window tax: introduced in ___   (ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER)","answer":"1696","why":{"en":"1696 is when it was introduced; 1851 is when it was abolished.","tr":"1696 getirildiği yıl; 1851 kaldırıldığı yıl.","fa":"۱۶۹۶ سال وضع مالیات است؛ ۱۸۵۱ سال لغو آن."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Sections, two pairs, a summary","tr":"Bölümler, iki çift, bir özet","fa":"بخش‌ها، دو جفت سؤال، یک خلاصه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 14-19: which section, A-G, contains each piece of information; a letter can be used more than once. Questions 20-21 and 22-23: choose TWO letters, A-E. Questions 24-26: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY.","tr":"Soru 14-19: her bilgi hangi bölümde (A-G); bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 20-21 ve 22-23: A-E arasından İKİ harf seç. Soru 24-26: bir özeti YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۴ تا ۱۹: هر اطلاعات در کدام بخش (A تا G) است؛ یک حرف را می‌شود بیش از یک بار به کار برد. سؤال‌های ۲۰-۲۱ و ۲۲-۲۳: دو حرف از A تا E انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۲۴ تا ۲۶: خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه کامل کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the whole passage quickly and write a three-word label beside each section.","tr":"Metnin tamamını hızla oku ve her bölümün yanına üç kelimelik bir etiket yaz.","fa":"کل متن را سریع بخوان و کنار هر بخش یک برچسب سه‌کلمه‌ای بنویس."},{"en":"For choose TWO, find the part of the passage the question is about and test all five options against it.","tr":"İKİ seçmeli sorularda sorunun ilgili olduğu kısmı bul ve beş seçeneğin hepsini ona göre test et.","fa":"برای «دو تا انتخاب کن»، بخشی از متن را که سؤال درباره‌اش است پیدا کن و هر پنج گزینه را با آن بسنج."},{"en":"Reject options that sound sensible but are not stated.","tr":"Mantıklı görünen ama metinde söylenmeyen seçenekleri ele.","fa":"گزینه‌هایی را که منطقی به نظر می‌رسند اما در متن نیامده‌اند رد کن."},{"en":"For the summary, find the paragraph it comes from and copy one word in its exact form.","tr":"Özet için hangi paragraftan geldiğini bul ve tek kelimeyi tam biçimiyle kopyala.","fa":"برای خلاصه، پاراگرافی را که از آن آمده پیدا کن و یک کلمه را به همان شکل دقیق کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"True in the world, not in the text","tr":"Dünyada doğru, metinde değil","fa":"در دنیا درست، در متن نه"},"body":{"en":"In choose TWO, distractors often state something you might believe (\"the laws were unclear\"). If the passage does not say it, it cannot be an answer, however reasonable it sounds.","tr":"İKİ seçmeli sorularda çeldiriciler çoğu zaman inanabileceğin bir şeyi söyler (\"yasalar belirsizdi\"). Metin bunu söylemiyorsa, ne kadar makul görünse de cevap olamaz.","fa":"در سؤال‌های «دو تا انتخاب کن»، گزینه‌های انحرافی اغلب چیزی می‌گویند که ممکن است باورش کنی («قانون‌ها مبهم بودند»). اگر متن آن را نگوید، هرچقدر هم منطقی باشد، جواب نیست."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One section question, step by step","tr":"Bir bölüm sorusu, adım adım","fa":"یک سؤالِ بخش، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which section contains the following information?","text":"Section C: \"...the workers were paid by the piece, so a fast weaver could earn twice as much as a slow one...\"","item":"a comparison of what different workers could earn","answer":"C","walk":[{"en":"The question asks for a detail: a comparison of earnings.","tr":"Soru bir ayrıntı istiyor: kazançların karşılaştırması.","fa":"سؤال یک جزئیات می‌خواهد: مقایسه‌ی درآمدها."},{"en":"\"Twice as much as\" is a comparison; \"earn\" matches earnings.","tr":"\"Twice as much as\" bir karşılaştırma; \"earn\", kazançla eşleşiyor.","fa":"«twice as much as» یک مقایسه است؛ «earn» با درآمد جور است."},{"en":"Even if Section C is mainly about weaving methods, it contains the detail: C.","tr":"C bölümü esas olarak dokuma yöntemleriyle ilgili olsa bile ayrıntı orada: C.","fa":"حتی اگر بخش C بیشتر درباره‌ی روش بافندگی باشد، این جزئیات در آن هست: C."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Passage: \"Sales fell after the tax rise, and later the shop moved to a cheaper street.\" Which TWO events are stated? A sales fell  B the tax rose  C the owner retired","options":["A and B","A and C","B and C"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Sales fell and the tax rose are both stated; nothing is said about the owner retiring.","tr":"Satışların düşmesi ve verginin artması söyleniyor; sahibin emekli olmasından söz yok.","fa":"کاهش فروش و افزایش مالیات هر دو گفته شده‌اند؛ درباره‌ی بازنشستگی صاحب مغازه حرفی نیست."}},"remember":{"en":"Label the sections, test every option against the text, and reject what is only reasonable.","tr":"Bölümleri etiketle, her seçeneği metne göre test et, yalnızca makul olanı ele.","fa":"بخش‌ها را برچسب بزن، هر گزینه را با متن بسنج و چیزی را که فقط منطقی است رد کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x09-r2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 2","title":{"en":"Free traders: smuggling on the eighteenth-century coast","tr":"Serbest tüccarlar: 18. yüzyıl kıyısında kaçakçılık","fa":"تاجران آزاد: قاچاق در سواحل قرن هجدهم"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-history"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.","passage":"Free traders: smuggling on the eighteenth-century coast\n\nA  In the eighteenth century, the coasts of southern and eastern England were busy at night. Small boats slipped onto quiet beaches, lanterns flashed from cliffs, and lines of men carried barrels and bales inland before dawn. Smuggling was not the work of a few outlaws but an industry, and those who took part often called themselves \"free traders\", a name that suggested they were doing nothing worse than avoiding an unfair tax. The goods they moved were the everyday luxuries of the period: tea, brandy, gin, tobacco and fine cloth. Most of them were not dangerous or forbidden in themselves; what made them illegal was simply the fact that no tax had been paid on them.\n\nB  The reason for this trade lay in government finance. Britain fought a series of expensive wars during the century, and one of the main ways of paying for them was to tax goods brought into the country. Duties on some items became extraordinarily high; at times the tax on tea was greater than the price of the tea itself. A smuggler who avoided the duty could therefore sell tea far more cheaply than an honest merchant and still make a large profit. Even after paying the boat crews, the carriers and the people who helped to hide the goods, the leaders of a successful run could expect to earn a small fortune. Historians cannot measure an illegal trade precisely, but some estimate that for a period more tea entered the country illegally than legally.\n\nC  The methods were well organised. Goods were bought in French ports or on the Channel Islands and loaded onto fast sailing boats, which crossed at night to avoid being seen. Signals from the shore told the crew whether it was safe to land. Once the cargo was on the beach, teams of labourers known as tubmen carried the barrels inland, often with one hanging on the chest and another on the back. The goods were then hidden until they could be sold, in caves, under the floors of farm buildings, and occasionally, it is said, in churches. From there they were carried by packhorse to inns and shops in the towns, and some cargoes reached London within a few days of landing.\n\nD  Smuggling could not have worked without the support of local communities. In poor coastal villages, a farm labourer might earn more in a single night carrying barrels than in a week of work in the fields, and few were willing to give up such an opportunity. Support also came from higher up. Landowners, doctors and even members of the clergy bought smuggled brandy and tea, and some invested money in the voyages. When smugglers were caught, it was often hard to punish them: magistrates who enjoyed cheap tea themselves were not eager to convict, and local juries frequently refused to find their neighbours guilty.\n\nE  The romantic image of the cheerful smuggler hides a darker side. Some gangs were large, armed and willing to use violence against anyone who threatened their business. In the 1740s, one notorious gang in the south of England captured two men who had agreed to give evidence against them and murdered them with great cruelty. The case shocked the country, and for a time public sympathy turned against the smugglers. Several members of the gang were hanged, and the authorities made a determined effort to break up other large groups. Even so, smaller gangs continued to operate along the coast for decades.\n\nF  Yet the forces responsible for stopping smugglers were small and badly equipped. On land, riding officers patrolled long stretches of coast alone on horseback, sometimes covering many miles in a night. At sea, a handful of armed revenue boats tried to intercept the smugglers' faster vessels. The officers were poorly paid, which made them easy to bribe, and an officer who was too successful could find himself threatened or attacked. Many simply looked the other way, and a few were known to have worked with the smugglers themselves.\n\nG  What finally reduced smuggling was not force but economics. In 1784 the government cut the duty on tea dramatically, from well over one hundred per cent to a small fraction of that, and almost overnight tea smuggling ceased to be worth the risk. After the long wars with France ended in 1815, more ships and sailors became available to guard the coast, and a national coast guard service was later created. Over the following decades, duties on many other goods were reduced as Britain moved towards freer trade, and the great age of the free traders slowly came to an end.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 14-19. Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"a comparison between the income from smuggling and from ordinary work","correct":3,"evidence":"might earn more in a single night carrying barrels than in a week of work in the fields","why":{"en":"D: one night carrying barrels paid more than a week in the fields.","tr":"D: bir gece fıçı taşımak, tarlada bir haftadan fazla kazandırıyordu.","fa":"D: یک شب حمل بشکه بیشتر از یک هفته کار در مزرعه درآمد داشت."},"trap":["TR-detail","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"a list of places where goods were concealed","correct":2,"evidence":"in caves, under the floors of farm buildings","why":{"en":"C: caves, farm buildings and churches. Concealed = hidden.","tr":"C: mağaralar, çiftlik binaları ve kiliseler. Concealed = gizlenmiş.","fa":"C: غارها، ساختمان‌های مزرعه و کلیساها. concealed یعنی پنهان‌شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"an explanation of why smuggled goods could be sold at a lower price","correct":1,"evidence":"could therefore sell tea far more cheaply than an honest merchant","why":{"en":"B: avoiding the duty let smugglers sell \"far more cheaply\".","tr":"B: vergiden kaçmak kaçakçıların \"çok daha ucuza\" satmasını sağlıyordu.","fa":"B: فرار از عوارض به قاچاقچی‌ها اجازه می‌داد «خیلی ارزان‌تر» بفروشند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"match","prompt":"reasons why the people employed to stop smuggling often failed","correct":5,"evidence":"The officers were poorly paid, which made them easy to bribe","why":{"en":"F: few officers, badly equipped, poorly paid and easy to bribe.","tr":"F: az sayıda, kötü donanımlı, düşük maaşlı ve kolayca rüşvet alan görevliler.","fa":"F: مأمورهای کم، با تجهیزات ضعیف، کم‌حقوق و رشوه‌پذیر."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":18,"kind":"match","prompt":"an event that made the public less sympathetic to smugglers","correct":4,"evidence":"for a time public sympathy turned against the smugglers","why":{"en":"E: the murders \"shocked the country\" and sympathy turned against the gangs.","tr":"E: cinayetler \"ülkeyi sarstı\" ve sempati çetelerin aleyhine döndü.","fa":"E: قتل‌ها «کشور را تکان داد» و همدلی مردم علیه باندها شد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to a change in the law that made smuggling less profitable","correct":6,"evidence":"In 1784 the government cut the duty on tea dramatically","why":{"en":"G: the 1784 cut in the tea duty meant smuggling was no longer \"worth the risk\".","tr":"G: 1784’te çay vergisinin düşürülmesi kaçakçılığı artık \"riske değmez\" hâle getirdi.","fa":"G: کاهش عوارض چای در ۱۷۸۴ باعث شد قاچاق دیگر «ارزش خطر را نداشته باشد»."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 20-21. Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":20,"n2":21,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO reasons does the writer give for why it was difficult to punish smugglers?","options":["A Juries often refused to find them guilty.","B The laws against smuggling were unclear.","C Some magistrates benefited from smuggling themselves.","D Witnesses were usually paid by the smugglers.","E The courts were a long way from the coast."],"correct":[0,2],"evidence":"magistrates who enjoyed cheap tea themselves were not eager to convict","trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-detail"],"why":{"en":"Section D: magistrates \"who enjoyed cheap tea themselves\" and juries that \"refused to find their neighbours guilty\". The other reasons are not in the passage.","tr":"D bölümü: \"kendileri de ucuz çaydan yararlanan\" yargıçlar ve \"komşularını suçlu bulmayı reddeden\" jüriler. Diğer nedenler metinde yok.","fa":"بخش D: قاضی‌هایی که «خودشان از چای ارزان لذت می‌بردند» و هیئت‌منصفه‌هایی که «همسایه‌هایشان را مجرم نمی‌شناختند». دلیل‌های دیگر در متن نیست."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 22-23. Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":22,"n2":23,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO statements about the decline of smuggling are true according to the passage?","options":["A It happened suddenly for all kinds of goods.","B It followed a large reduction in the tax on tea.","C Smugglers moved their business to France.","D More ships could patrol the coast after a war ended.","E The public began to support the riding officers."],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"In 1784 the government cut the duty on tea dramatically","trap":["TR-samewords","TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"Section G: the tea duty was cut dramatically, and after 1815 \"more ships and sailors became available\". For other goods the decline was slow (\"over the following decades\").","tr":"G bölümü: çay vergisi büyük ölçüde düşürüldü ve 1815’ten sonra \"daha fazla gemi ve denizci kullanılabilir oldu\". Diğer mallarda düşüş yavaştı (\"sonraki on yıllarda\").","fa":"بخش G: عوارض چای به‌شدت کم شد و بعد از ۱۸۱۵ «کشتی‌ها و ملوان‌های بیشتری در دسترس قرار گرفتند». برای کالاهای دیگر کاهش کند بود («در دهه‌های بعد»)."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 24-26. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"From the beach to the town","questions":[{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Boats crossed the sea at ___ so that they would not be seen.","accept":["night"],"limit":1,"evidence":"which crossed at night to avoid being seen","why":{"en":"\"Crossed at night to avoid being seen\".","tr":"\"Görülmemek için gece geçtiler\".","fa":"«شب‌ها رد می‌شدند تا دیده نشوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"On the beach, men called tubmen carried the ___ inland.","accept":["barrels"],"limit":1,"evidence":"teams of labourers known as tubmen carried the barrels inland","why":{"en":"\"Tubmen carried the barrels inland\". Plural.","tr":"\"Tubmen fıçıları içeri taşıdı\". Çoğul.","fa":"«تابمن‌ها بشکه‌ها را به داخل خشکی می‌بردند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Goods were then taken by ___ to inns and shops in the towns.","accept":["packhorse"],"limit":1,"evidence":"they were carried by packhorse to inns and shops","why":{"en":"\"Carried by packhorse to inns and shops in the towns\". One word.","tr":"\"Yük atlarıyla kasabalardaki hanlara ve dükkânlara taşındı\". Tek kelime.","fa":"«با اسب بارکش به مسافرخانه‌ها و مغازه‌های شهر برده می‌شدند». یک کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x09-r2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Magistrates were not eager to convict.\" To convict someone is to...","options":["let them go free","pay them for information","decide officially that they are guilty"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Convict = find guilty in a court.","tr":"Convict = mahkemede suçlu bulmak.","fa":"convict یعنی در دادگاه مجرم شناختن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A question asks for \"places where goods were concealed\". Which words in a passage would match?","options":["were sold in shops","were hidden in caves","were bought in France"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Concealed = hidden.","tr":"Concealed = gizlenmiş.","fa":"concealed یعنی پنهان‌شده."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"In a choose-TWO question, option C sounds very likely but you cannot find it in the passage. What do you do?","options":["Do not choose it","Choose it because it is likely","Choose it if you have time left"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Only what the passage states can be an answer.","tr":"Yalnızca metnin söylediği şey cevap olabilir.","fa":"فقط چیزی که متن می‌گوید می‌تواند جواب باشد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":2,"prompt":"Text: \"Prices of coffee fell overnight; for sugar and cocoa, the change took decades.\" Option: \"Prices of all goods fell suddenly.\" Is it correct?","options":["Yes: prices fell","Not given","No: only coffee fell suddenly"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Overnight\" refers to coffee only; the other goods changed slowly.","tr":"\"Bir gecede\" yalnızca kahveyi anlatıyor; diğer mallar yavaş değişti.","fa":"«یک‌شبه» فقط درباره‌ی قهوه است؛ کالاهای دیگر کند تغییر کردند."}}],"id":"c-x09-r2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 2: workplace advice","tr":"GT Reading Section 2: iş yeri tavsiyeleri","fa":"GT Reading Section 2: توصیه‌های محیط کار"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete sentences and notes on two pieces of workplace advice, using one word from the text in its exact form.","tr":"Bu derste iş yeriyle ilgili iki tavsiye metninde cümleleri ve notları, metinden tek bir kelimeyi tam biçimiyle kullanarak tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها و یادداشت‌های دو متن توصیه‌ای درباره‌ی محیط کار را با یک کلمه از متن، به همان شکل دقیق، کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: new team leaders and resigning well","tr":"Bu sınav: yeni ekip liderleri ve düzgün istifa","fa":"این آزمون: سرپرست‌های تازه و استعفای درست"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 2 is always about work. Advice on running a team and on managing your career are two of its most frequent text types.","tr":"GT Section 2 her zaman işle ilgilidir. Ekip yönetimi ve kariyer yönetimi üzerine tavsiyeler bu bölümün en sık çıkan iki metin türüdür.","fa":"GT Section 2 همیشه درباره‌ی کار است. توصیه درباره‌ی اداره‌ی تیم و مدیریت مسیر شغلی دو نوع پرتکرار متن در این بخش‌اند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x09-r2gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT2-business","GT2-career","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Advice for leading a team and for leaving a job","tr":"Ekip yönetmek ve işten ayrılmak için tavsiyeler","fa":"توصیه‌هایی برای رهبری تیم و ترک کار"},"asks":{"en":"Two pieces of workplace advice: an article for new team leaders (listening, goals, trust, risks, looking after yourself) and a guide to resigning well (telling your manager, notice, handover, behaviour, goodbyes).","tr":"İş yeriyle ilgili iki tavsiye metni: yeni ekip liderleri için bir makale (dinlemek, hedefler, güven, riskler, kendine iyi bakmak) ve düzgün istifa etmek için bir rehber (yöneticine söylemek, ihbar süresi, devir teslim, davranış, vedalaşma).","fa":"دو متن توصیه‌ای درباره‌ی محیط کار: مقاله‌ای برای سرپرست‌های تازه‌کار (گوش دادن، هدف‌ها، اعتماد، ریسک، مراقبت از خود) و راهنمایی برای درست استعفا دادن (گفتن به مدیر، مهلت اعلام، تحویل کار، رفتار، خداحافظی)."},"fields":["First weeks","Goals","Trust","Risks and mistakes","Workload","Notice period","Handover","Leaving"],"words":[{"a":"individually","b":"one by one / each person alone","tr":"tek tek","fa":"تک‌تک"},{"a":"goals","b":"targets / what is expected","tr":"hedefler","fa":"هدف‌ها"},{"a":"regularly","b":"often / not only once a year","tr":"düzenli olarak","fa":"مرتب"},{"a":"delegate","b":"give tasks to others","tr":"görev devretmek","fa":"کار را واگذار کردن"},{"a":"in confidence","b":"privately / it stays between you","tr":"gizlilik içinde","fa":"محرمانه"},{"a":"resign","b":"leave your job / hand in your notice","tr":"istifa etmek","fa":"استعفا دادن"},{"a":"notice period","b":"how long you must work after resigning","tr":"ihbar süresi","fa":"مهلت اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"handover","b":"notes for the person taking over","tr":"devir teslim","fa":"تحویل کار"},{"a":"reference","b":"what a former employer says about you","tr":"referans","fa":"معرفی‌نامه"},{"a":"constructive","b":"helpful / aimed at improvement","tr":"yapıcı","fa":"سازنده"},{"a":"stated in","b":"written in / given in","tr":"... belirtilmiş","fa":"در ... آمده"}],"traps":[{"en":"The gap must be a word from the text in the right form. If the text says \"write them down\", \"written\" is not in the text, so the question cannot want it.","tr":"Boşluk metinden, doğru biçimde bir kelime olmalı. Metin \"write them down\" diyorsa \"written\" metinde yoktur; soru onu isteyemez.","fa":"جای خالی باید کلمه‌ای از متن با شکل درست باشد. اگر متن می‌گوید «write them down»، «written» در متن نیست، پس سؤال آن را نمی‌خواهد."},{"en":"Similar words close together: \"every week\" (team meeting) and \"every two weeks\" (one-to-one talk). Check which topic the sentence is about.","tr":"Birbirine yakın benzer ifadeler: \"her hafta\" (ekip toplantısı) ve \"iki haftada bir\" (birebir görüşme). Cümlenin hangi konuyla ilgili olduğuna bak.","fa":"عبارت‌های شبیه نزدیک هم: «هر هفته» (جلسه‌ی تیم) و «هر دو هفته یک بار» (گفتگوی دونفره). ببین جمله درباره‌ی کدام موضوع است."}],"example":{"text":"\"Keep a record of every meeting with your mentor, and share it with your manager each term.\"","item":"Sentence: Notes on mentoring meetings should be shared with your ___.","answer":"manager","why":{"en":"\"Share it with your manager\": copy the word exactly.","tr":"\"Yöneticinle paylaş\": kelimeyi aynen kopyala.","fa":"«با مدیرت به اشتراک بگذار»: کلمه را دقیق کپی کن."}}},{"id":"GT2-business","ctx":["GT2-business"],"title":{"en":"Running a team or a small business","tr":"Bir ekibi ya da küçük bir işletmeyi yönetmek","fa":"اداره‌ی یک تیم یا یک کسب‌وکار کوچک"},"asks":{"en":"Workplace guides on meetings, projects, delegation, marketing, flexible working or types of training. Sentence and note completion test the advice and the steps.","tr":"Toplantılar, projeler, görev devri, pazarlama, esnek çalışma ya da eğitim türleri üzerine iş yeri rehberleri. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri ve adımları sınar.","fa":"راهنماهای محیط کار درباره‌ی جلسه، پروژه، واگذاری کار، بازاریابی، کار منعطف یا انواع آموزش. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها و مرحله‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Before a meeting, send the ___ to everyone.","Give tasks to staff who can do them ___.","Flexible hours must be agreed with your ___.","Training: on the job · external course · online"],"words":[{"a":"agenda","b":"list of points for the meeting","tr":"gündem","fa":"دستور جلسه"},{"a":"delegate","b":"give a task to someone else","tr":"görev devretmek","fa":"واگذار کردن"},{"a":"deadline","b":"the date it must be done by","tr":"son tarih","fa":"مهلت"},{"a":"budget","b":"the money available","tr":"bütçe","fa":"بودجه"},{"a":"priorities","b":"what matters most","tr":"öncelikler","fa":"اولویت‌ها"},{"a":"minutes","b":"written record of a meeting","tr":"toplantı tutanağı","fa":"صورت‌جلسه"},{"a":"colleague","b":"co-worker","tr":"iş arkadaşı","fa":"همکار"},{"a":"line manager","b":"the person you report to","tr":"bağlı olduğun yönetici","fa":"مدیر مستقیم"},{"a":"flexible hours","b":"choose when you start and finish","tr":"esnek çalışma saatleri","fa":"ساعت کاری منعطف"},{"a":"client","b":"customer","tr":"müşteri","fa":"مشتری"},{"a":"promote","b":"advertise / market","tr":"tanıtmak","fa":"تبلیغ کردن"},{"a":"progress","b":"how far the work has got","tr":"ilerleme","fa":"پیشرفت"}],"traps":[{"en":"The sentence to complete is a paraphrase; the gap word is copied from the text.","tr":"Tamamlanacak cümle başka sözcüklerle yazılmıştır; boşluktaki kelime metinden kopyalanır.","fa":"جمله‌ای که کامل می‌کنی با کلمه‌های دیگر نوشته شده؛ کلمه‌ی جای خالی از متن کپی می‌شود."},{"en":"Lists of advice: the question asks about one step (\"before the meeting\"); the text lists several.","tr":"Tavsiye listeleri: soru tek bir adımı sorar (\"toplantıdan önce\"); metin birkaçını sıralar.","fa":"فهرست توصیه‌ها: سؤال درباره‌ی یک مرحله است («قبل از جلسه»)؛ متن چند مرحله را می‌شمارد."}],"example":{"text":"Circulate the minutes within 24 hours, while decisions are still fresh. Each action point should name one person, not a whole department.","item":"Sentence: Each action point should name a single ___.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"person","why":{"en":"\"Name one person, not a whole department\": a single person.","tr":"\"Bütün bir bölümü değil, tek bir kişiyi yaz\": a single person.","fa":"«یک نفر را نام ببر، نه کل یک بخش را»: a single person."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-business"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT2-career","ctx":["GT2-career"],"title":{"en":"Job and career guides","tr":"İş ve kariyer rehberleri","fa":"راهنمای کار و مسیر شغلی"},"asks":{"en":"Guides for job seekers and employees: CVs, interviews, promotion, resigning, freelance work, apprenticeships. Sentence and note completion test the advice.","tr":"İş arayanlar ve çalışanlar için rehberler: özgeçmiş, mülakat, terfi, istifa, serbest çalışma, çıraklık. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri sınar.","fa":"راهنما برای کارجوها و کارمندها: رزومه، مصاحبه، ترفیع، استعفا، کار آزاد، کارآموزی حرفه‌ای. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Keep your CV to ___ pages.","Research the company before the ___.","Give your employer written ___ when you resign.","Freelancers must keep records for ___."],"words":[{"a":"CV","b":"career summary / résumé","tr":"özgeçmiş","fa":"رزومه"},{"a":"applicant","b":"candidate / person applying","tr":"başvuran","fa":"متقاضی"},{"a":"vacancy","b":"an open job","tr":"açık pozisyon","fa":"موقعیت شغلی خالی"},{"a":"interview","b":"meeting with the employer","tr":"mülakat","fa":"مصاحبه"},{"a":"resign","b":"leave your job / hand in your notice","tr":"istifa etmek","fa":"استعفا دادن"},{"a":"notice period","b":"time between resigning and leaving","tr":"ihbar süresi","fa":"مدت اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"promotion","b":"moving up to a higher job","tr":"terfi","fa":"ترفیع"},{"a":"freelance","b":"self-employed / working for yourself","tr":"serbest","fa":"آزادکار"},{"a":"apprenticeship","b":"training while you work","tr":"çıraklık","fa":"کارآموزی حرفه‌ای"},{"a":"references","b":"people who will recommend you","tr":"referanslar","fa":"معرف‌ها"},{"a":"salary","b":"pay / earnings","tr":"maaş","fa":"حقوق"},{"a":"recent","b":"latest / most up to date","tr":"en son","fa":"جدیدترین"}],"traps":[{"en":"Advice for different stages: \"before the interview\" and \"after the interview\" are different paragraphs.","tr":"Farklı aşamalar için tavsiyeler: \"mülakattan önce\" ve \"mülakattan sonra\" farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"توصیه برای مرحله‌های مختلف: «قبل از مصاحبه» و «بعد از مصاحبه» در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."},{"en":"The gap needs a word from the text, even if a synonym feels more natural.","tr":"Boşluk metinden bir kelime ister; eş anlamlısı daha doğal gelse bile.","fa":"جای خالی کلمه‌ای از متن را می‌خواهد، حتی اگر مترادفش طبیعی‌تر به نظر برسد."}],"example":{"text":"Most employers spend less than a minute on each CV, so keep yours to two pages and put your most recent job first.","item":"Sentence: Put your most ___ job first.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"recent","why":{"en":"\"Put your most recent job first.\" Copy recent; do not change it to \"latest\".","tr":"\"En son işini en başa koy.\" recent kelimesini kopyala; \"latest\" diye değiştirme.","fa":"«جدیدترین شغلت را اول بنویس». کلمه‌ی recent را کپی کن؛ به latest تغییرش نده."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-career"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-career","n":18,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Sentences, then notes","tr":"Önce cümleler, sonra notlar","fa":"اول جمله، بعد یادداشت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 15-21: complete sentences on the first text. Questions 22-27: complete notes on the second text. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text each time. The answers follow the order of each text.","tr":"Soru 15-21: birinci metinle ilgili cümleleri tamamla. Soru 22-27: ikinci metinle ilgili notları tamamla. Her seferinde metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİME yaz. Cevaplar her metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۵ تا ۲۱: جمله‌های متن اول را کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۷: یادداشت‌های متن دوم را کامل کن. هر بار فقط یک کلمه از متن بنویس. جواب‌ها به ترتیب هر متن می‌آیند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Use the subheadings of the text to find the right section quickly.","tr":"Doğru bölümü hızla bulmak için metnin ara başlıklarını kullan.","fa":"برای پیدا کردن سریع بخش درست از زیرعنوان‌های متن استفاده کن."},{"en":"Read the sentence and predict the word class: an adverb after a verb, a noun after \"a\" or \"the\".","tr":"Cümleyi oku ve kelime türünü tahmin et: fiilden sonra zarf, \"a\" ya da \"the\"den sonra isim.","fa":"جمله را بخوان و نوع کلمه را حدس بزن: بعد از فعل قید، بعد از «a» یا «the» اسم."},{"en":"Find the matching idea in the text; the words around it will be paraphrased.","tr":"Metinde aynı fikri bul; etrafındaki kelimeler başka biçimde söylenmiş olacak.","fa":"ایده‌ی مشابه را در متن پیدا کن؛ کلمه‌های اطرافش بازگویی شده‌اند."},{"en":"Copy the word exactly; check spelling and plural.","tr":"Kelimeyi aynen kopyala; yazımı ve çoğulu kontrol et.","fa":"کلمه را دقیق کپی کن؛ املا و جمع را چک کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Grammar tells you the word","tr":"Dilbilgisi kelimeyi söyler","fa":"دستور زبان کلمه را نشان می‌دهد"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The sentence","The gap needs"],"tr":["Cümle","Boşluk ister"],"fa":["جمله","جای خالی می‌خواهد"]},"rows":[["arrive ___ for the interview","an adverb (how? when?)"],["hand in your ___ to HR","a noun"],["avoid ___ with colleagues","a noun, often plural"],["try to ___ your workload","a verb in the base form"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One sentence, step by step","tr":"Bir cümle, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the sentence below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","text":"\"When you join, you will be given a security pass. Keep it with you at all times and show it at the main gate.\"","item":"Staff must show their ___ at the main gate.","answer":"pass","walk":[{"en":"After \"their\", the gap needs a noun.","tr":"\"their\"den sonra boşluk bir isim istiyor.","fa":"بعد از «their» جای خالی اسم می‌خواهد."},{"en":"\"Show it at the main gate\": \"it\" refers to the security pass.","tr":"\"Ana kapıda göster\": \"it\" güvenlik kartına işaret ediyor.","fa":"«دمِ در اصلی نشانش بده»: «it» به کارت ورود برمی‌گردد."},{"en":"One word only: pass (not \"security pass\").","tr":"Yalnızca bir kelime: pass (\"security pass\" değil).","fa":"فقط یک کلمه: pass (نه «security pass»)."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Breaks should be taken away from your desk.\" Sentence: \"Staff should not take breaks at their ___.\" What do you write?","options":["desks","desk","table"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Copy the word in the form the text uses: desk, not desks. Table means something similar but is not in the text.","tr":"Kelimeyi metnin kullandığı biçimde kopyala: desks değil, desk. Table benzer anlamda ama metinde yok.","fa":"کلمه را به همان شکلی که متن به کار برده کپی کن: desk، نه desks. table معنی مشابهی دارد اما در متن نیست."}},"remember":{"en":"Predict the word class, find the paraphrase, copy the exact word.","tr":"Kelime türünü tahmin et, eş anlamlıyı bul, tam kelimeyi kopyala.","fa":"نوع کلمه را حدس بزن، بازگویی را پیدا کن، کلمه‌ی دقیق را کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x09-r2-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 2","title":{"en":"Leading a team and leaving a job","tr":"Ekip yönetmek ve işten ayrılmak","fa":"رهبری تیم و ترک کار"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT2-business","GT2-career"],"texts":[{"title":"Leading a team for the first time","kind":"advice article","body":"Being promoted to lead a team is exciting, but many new managers find the first few months harder than they expected. The skills that made you good at your old job are not always the ones you need now. Instead of being judged on your own work, you will be judged on what the whole team achieves. Here is some practical advice from experienced team leaders in a range of industries.\n\nListen before you change anything\nIt is tempting to arrive with a list of improvements. Resist it. Spend your first few weeks meeting each member of the team individually and asking what works well and what does not. People are far more willing to accept change when they feel that their views have been heard.\n\nBe clear about expectations\nProblems often start when team members are unsure what is expected of them. Agree clear goals with each person, and write them down, so that everyone knows how their work will be judged. Review these goals regularly rather than waiting for the annual appraisal. A short conversation once a month is usually enough to keep everyone on track.\n\nBuild trust\nTrust is built slowly and lost quickly. Keep the promises you make, admit your mistakes openly and give credit to the people who did the work. If you are leading former colleagues, you may need to accept that some relationships will change. Friendship is valuable, but you cannot treat friends differently from the rest of the team.\n\nLet people take risks\nA team that is afraid of making mistakes will never try anything new. Make it clear that sensible risks are welcome, and when something goes wrong, focus on what can be learned rather than on who is to blame.\n\nLook after yourself\nNew managers often work extremely long hours in an attempt to do everything themselves. This is not sustainable. Learn to delegate tasks, even when you could do them faster yourself, and ask your own manager for support. Many organisations also offer mentoring schemes, in which an experienced leader meets new managers once a month to discuss problems in confidence."},{"title":"Leaving your job the right way","kind":"guide","body":"However happy you are to be moving on, the way you leave a job can affect your career for years. Former employers are often asked for references, and in many industries people meet the same colleagues again and again.\n\nTell your manager first\nYour manager should hear the news from you in person, not from a colleague or a social media post. Ask for a private meeting, explain your decision briefly and politely, and follow it up with a short letter of resignation.\n\nCheck your notice period\nYour contract will state how much notice you must give. This is commonly one month, but it can be longer in senior roles. In some cases an employer may agree to let you leave earlier, but you should not assume this. Leaving before the end of your notice period without agreement could mean losing part of your final salary.\n\nPrepare a handover\nIn your last weeks, write clear notes on the work you are responsible for: ongoing projects, important contacts and where files are kept. A good handover makes life easier for whoever takes over your role, and it will be remembered. If possible, spend some time with your replacement, or with the colleague who will cover your work, and introduce them to the people they will need to know.\n\nStay professional\nKeep working to the same standard until your final day. Avoid criticising the company or your colleagues, even if you are asked for your opinion. If your employer offers an exit interview, give honest but constructive feedback. Focus on what could be improved for the people who stay, not on personal complaints.\n\nSay goodbye\nBefore you go, thank the people who have helped you and make sure they have your personal contact details. Many people find that former colleagues later become clients, partners or even employers."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 15-21. Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"sentence","questions":[{"n":15,"kind":"gap","prompt":"New team leaders are judged on what the whole ___ achieves.","accept":["team"],"limit":1,"evidence":"judged on what the whole team achieves","why":{"en":"\"You will be judged on what the whole team achieves.\"","tr":"\"Bütün ekibin başardıklarına göre değerlendirileceksin.\"","fa":"«بر اساس دستاورد کل تیم سنجیده می‌شوی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"gap","prompt":"In the first weeks, a new leader should meet each team member ___.","accept":["individually"],"limit":1,"evidence":"meeting each member of the team individually","why":{"en":"\"Meeting each member of the team individually\". Copy the adverb.","tr":"\"Ekibin her üyesiyle tek tek görüşmek\". Zarfı kopyala.","fa":"«دیدار با تک‌تک اعضای تیم». قید را کپی کن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Goals agreed with each person should be reviewed ___, not only once a year.","accept":["regularly"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Review these goals regularly","why":{"en":"\"Review these goals regularly rather than waiting for the annual appraisal.\"","tr":"\"Bu hedefleri yıllık değerlendirmeyi beklemeden düzenli olarak gözden geçir.\"","fa":"«این هدف‌ها را مرتب بازبینی کن، نه اینکه منتظر ارزیابی سالانه بمانی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Leaders should give ___ to the people who actually did the work.","accept":["credit"],"limit":1,"evidence":"give credit to the people who did the work","why":{"en":"\"Give credit to the people who did the work\".","tr":"\"İşi yapan insanların hakkını ver\".","fa":"«اعتبار کار را به کسانی بده که آن را انجام دادند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"A team that fears ___ will not try anything new.","accept":["mistakes"],"limit":1,"evidence":"A team that is afraid of making mistakes will never try anything new","why":{"en":"\"Afraid of making mistakes\" = fears mistakes. Plural.","tr":"\"Hata yapmaktan korkan\" = hatadan korkan. Çoğul.","fa":"«از اشتباه کردن می‌ترسد» یعنی از اشتباه می‌ترسد. جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"New managers should learn to ___ tasks to others.","accept":["delegate"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Learn to delegate tasks","why":{"en":"\"Learn to delegate tasks, even when you could do them faster yourself.\"","tr":"\"Kendin daha hızlı yapabilsen bile görev devretmeyi öğren.\"","fa":"«یاد بگیر کارها را به دیگران بسپاری، حتی وقتی خودت سریع‌تر انجامشان می‌دهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"In a mentoring scheme, an experienced leader meets new managers every ___.","accept":["month"],"limit":1,"evidence":"meets new managers once a month","why":{"en":"\"Once a month\" = every month.","tr":"\"Ayda bir\" = her ay.","fa":"«ماهی یک بار» یعنی هر ماه."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 22-27. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Leaving your job","questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Telling your employer · speak to your manager in a ___ meeting","accept":["private"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Ask for a private meeting","why":{"en":"\"Ask for a private meeting\", not through colleagues or social media.","tr":"\"Özel bir görüşme iste\", iş arkadaşları ya da sosyal medya aracılığıyla değil.","fa":"«درخواست یک جلسه‌ی خصوصی کن»، نه از طریق همکارها یا شبکه‌های اجتماعی."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Telling your employer · confirm it with a short ___ of resignation","accept":["letter"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a short letter of resignation","why":{"en":"\"Follow it up with a short letter of resignation\".","tr":"\"Ardından kısa bir istifa mektubu gönder\".","fa":"«بعدش یک نامه‌ی کوتاه استعفا بفرست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Notice · the length is stated in your ___","accept":["contract"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Your contract will state how much notice you must give","why":{"en":"\"Your contract will state how much notice you must give.\"","tr":"\"Sözleşmen ne kadar önceden haber vermen gerektiğini belirtir.\"","fa":"«قراردادت می‌گوید چقدر پیش‌تر باید خبر بدهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Notice · leaving early without agreement may cost part of your final ___","accept":["salary"],"limit":1,"evidence":"losing part of your final salary","why":{"en":"\"Could mean losing part of your final salary.\"","tr":"\"Son maaşının bir kısmını kaybetmek anlamına gelebilir.\"","fa":"«ممکن است یعنی بخشی از آخرین حقوقت را از دست بدهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Handover · write notes on projects, contacts and where ___ are kept","accept":["files"],"limit":1,"evidence":"where files are kept","why":{"en":"\"Where files are kept\". Plural.","tr":"\"Dosyaların nerede tutulduğu\". Çoğul.","fa":"«پرونده‌ها کجا نگه داشته می‌شوند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":27,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Last days · in an exit interview, give honest but ___ feedback","accept":["constructive"],"limit":1,"evidence":"give honest but constructive feedback","why":{"en":"\"Give honest but constructive feedback\".","tr":"\"Dürüst ama yapıcı geri bildirim ver\".","fa":"«بازخورد صادقانه اما سازنده بده»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x09-r2-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Learn to delegate tasks.\" To delegate is to...","options":["give work to other people","finish work early","check other people’s work"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Delegate = pass a task to someone else.","tr":"Delegate = bir işi başkasına devretmek.","fa":"delegate یعنی سپردن کار به کس دیگر."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A note says \"how long you must work after resigning\". Which phrase in a guide means this?","options":["handover","exit interview","notice period"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Notice period = the time between resigning and leaving.","tr":"Notice period = istifa ile ayrılış arasındaki süre.","fa":"notice period یعنی فاصله‌ی بین استعفا و رفتن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Sentence: \"Leaders should treat all team members ___.\" What kind of word do you need?","options":["a noun, such as equality","an adverb, such as equally","a verb, such as equal"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"After \"treat all team members\", the gap describes how: an adverb.","tr":"\"treat all team members\"tan sonra boşluk nasıl olduğunu anlatır: bir zarf.","fa":"بعد از «treat all team members» جای خالی می‌گوید «چطور»: یک قید."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Speak to your line manager first.\" Note: \"First tell your ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". Which answer is acceptable?","options":["manager","line manager","boss"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Line manager\" is two words; \"boss\" is not in the text. Manager fits.","tr":"\"Line manager\" iki kelime; \"boss\" metinde yok. Manager uyuyor.","fa":"«line manager» دو کلمه است؛ «boss» در متن نیست. manager درست است."}}],"id":"c-x09-r2-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r2"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
